%% showcase: stateDiagram with composite states
%% prose: An order's life cycle. Start and end dots belong to their scope, so the composite Fulfilment has its own; a choice diamond splits on payment, and a fork and join run packing and invoicing side by side. Transitions may end on a composite's box, and notes sit beside their state.
%% approx: Layout is mmd's layered algorithm, not dagre, so states sit in different places than mermaid puts them.
%% approx: A composite state's title sits at its top-left inside the box, not in a separate title band.
%% approx: Notes are joined to their state by a dashed line; in a left-right flow a note goes above or below its state instead of left or right.
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Draft
    Draft --> Submitted : submit
    Submitted --> paid
    state paid <<choice>>
    paid --> Fulfilment : payment cleared
    paid --> Draft : declined
    state Fulfilment {
        [*] --> Picking
        Picking --> split
        state split <<fork>>
        split --> Packing
        split --> Invoicing
        state done <<join>>
        Packing --> done
        Invoicing --> done
        done --> [*]
    }
    Fulfilment --> Shipped : hand to carrier
    Shipped --> Delivered
    Delivered --> [*]
    Shipped : tracked
    Shipped : insured
    note right of Draft : editable by the customer
    note left of Shipped
        Carrier updates
        arrive by webhook
    end note
    classDef warn fill:#fde68a,stroke:#b45309
    class paid warn
